    "recommendations": "• Clear or thin the dense vegetation areas to open sight lines along the access drive so responders can see the structures and move between them without obstruction.\n• Trim vegetation along both sides of the access drive to maintain a clear travel path wide enough for emergency vehicles.\n• Install a reflective address marker at the entrance to the access drive so responders can identify the property quickly from the road.\n• Mark the driveway entrance clearly to distinguish it from neighboring access points, especially under low-light or smoky conditions.\n• Keep the walkway between the main residence and the detached structure clear of vegetation overgrowth so responders can move on foot between buildings.\n• Designate a flat, open staging area within the open lawn area and keep it free of parked vehicles, equipment, and stored materials so arriving units have a place to set up.\n• Because there is only one access point, avoid blocking the driveway entrance or access drive with vehicles, trailers, or stored items at any time.\n• Install a turnaround area or a pull-out space along the access drive to allow emergency vehicles to reposition without backing out to the road.\n• Thin dense vegetation near the detached structure so responders can reach and work around all sides of that building.\n• Keep any gates on the property unlocked or provide a Knox-Box or coded lock so responders are not delayed accessing the site."
  },
