    "recommendations": "• Trim tree branches that hang directly over or touch the roof and walls of the structure.\n• Thin the tree clusters nearest to the structure to create open gaps between individual trees.\n• Remove shrubs and low-growing plants that grow directly against the foundation or walls of the structure.\n• Thin scattered trees around the structure so their branches do not touch or overlap with each other.\n• Cut back mixed vegetation growing close to the structure on all sides to create open ground between plants and the building.\n• Clear ground vegetation within the immediate area surrounding the structure, leaving bare soil or very short grass.\n• Trim branches and shrubs along the driveway so vehicles can pass through without obstruction.\n• Keep the driveway surface clear of fallen branches, leaves, and debris that could block access.\n• Remove or cut back vegetation along the edges of the driveway that narrows the travel lane.\n• Thin shrubs scattered around the property so they are separated from each other and from the structure.\n• Keep the single access route free of any vegetation that could block emergency vehicle entry or exit at any point along its length.\n• Remove dead branches, dry grass, and fallen leaves from around the base of trees near the structure."
